<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 223 0 R
/E (     A total of 19 student teams, comprising 38 students, participated in the event. Students presented working models based on operational amplifiers, IC 555 timers, filters, waveform generators, voltage regulators, instrumentation amplifiers, phase-locked loops, and other Linear Integrated Circuit applications. Faculty members evaluated the projects based on technical understanding, circuit implementation, innovation, documentation, and presentation skills. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
357 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 223 0 R
/E (    The event encouraged interactive learning, allowing participants to explain the design, operation, and applications of their projects. Live demonstrations, technical discussions, and question-and-answer sessions enabled students to strengthen their practical knowledge while improving communication and presentation skills. The Open House successfully bridged the gap between theoretical learning and real-world engineering applications.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
