817 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 241 0 R
/T (   The NSS Orientation Program 2026 was organized to introduce new students to the values and objectives of the National Service Scheme. The program began with a Lamp Lighting ceremony, followed by an introduction to NSS and the NSS Song. Motivational speeches by the Principal and faculty members inspired students to participate in community service. A video and PPT showcased the activities and achievements of NSS GEC Patan, while senior volunteers shared their experiences and the impact of NSS on their personal growth. The program concluded with a Vote of Thanks, encouraging students to actively contribute to society through NSS.)
/E (   The NSS Orientation Program 2026 was organized to introduce new students to the values and objectives of the National Service Scheme. The program began with a Lamp Lighting ceremony, followed by an introduction to NSS and the NSS Song. Motivational speeches by the Principal and faculty members inspired students to participate in community service. A video and PPT showcased the activities and achievements of NSS GEC Patan, while senior volunteers shared their experiences and the impact of NSS on their personal growth. The program concluded with a Vote of Thanks, encouraging students to actively contribute to society through NSS.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
818 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 241 0 R
/E (    The World No Tobacco Day awareness program was organized online on 31st May 2026 through Google Meet to educate students about the harmful effects of tobacco and promote a healthy, addiction-free lifestyle. The session included an informative presentation on tobacco consumption in Gujarat, its health risks, and the importance of prevention. Participants also took the No Tobacco Pledge and were motivated by an inspiring address from a faculty member to adopt healthy habits and spread awareness. The program concluded with a Vote of Thanks, successfully encouraging students to contribute towards a tobacco-free society.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
